  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler as an IProvisioningHandler in the L2 control-plane. Per Option A (SESSION 4 design decision): EXTEND task 084's shipped canonical manifest with a NEW top-level list `per_env_settings:` for per-env-literal App Service settings (URIs, TenantId, ContainerTypeId, WebhookSigningKey, WebhookClientState — values that shouldn't be KV secrets OR needed to bootstrap KV access). Extend `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` to emit these per-env lines into the SAME existing `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` output alongside the KV-ref lines. H4b handler is a ~100-line thin C# wrapper: resolves per-env values from HandlerEnvelope.Parameters.NonSecret; shells to `pwsh scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/generated/Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1 -VaultName X -AppServiceName Y -TenantId Z ...`; polls `/healthz` with 8-min backoff via `IHealthzProbe`; on failure parses container docker logs via Kudu API for `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException:` line → extracts IOptions module name for actionable diagnostic. This kills the F20 progressive-fail-fast chain by applying ALL required BFF app settings in ONE batch (SINGLE `az webapp config appsettings set --settings @settings` call → ONE App Service restart cycle) — the existing generator already does batched write; task 201 fills the per-env-literal gap.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in: the L2 4-project scaffold (`Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.{Api,Worker,Core,Tests}`); the `IProvisioningHandler` contract (returns `HandlerResult`, NOT exceptions for domain failures); the shipped canonical secret-catalog manifest + generator (task 084 landed 2026-08-17 `70abd9992`); the existing `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` batched app-settings-write mechanism (verified via SESSION 4 recon — batches per slot via `az webapp config appsettings set --settings @settings`); App Service KV-ref format `@Microsoft.KeyVault(VaultName=X;SecretName=Y)`; .NET IOptions `.ValidateOnStart()` fail-fast pattern (~40 modules in BFF); the 3-file DI dance (`HandlerIds.cs` + `HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs` + `.Worker\Program.cs`); the H4 exemplar (H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs — the canonical reference for HandlerResult semantics + idempotency). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Files exist and the following contract is satisfied: (a) canonical manifest at `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` extended with NEW top-level list `per_env_settings:` (see schema in constraints below); (b) `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` extended to validate `per_env_settings:` shape + emit per-env-literal lines into `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` alongside existing KV-ref lines (SAME output file — not a sibling); (c) `-DryRun` + `-Verify` still exit 0; (d) `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core\Handlers\BulkAppSettings\H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` implements `IProvisioningHandler`; (e) new seams: `IProcessRunner` (or reuse if exists — check first) + `IHealthzProbe` + `IContainerLogFetcher`; (f) all seam impls in same `.Core\Handlers\BulkAppSettings\` folder; (g) new `HandlerIds.H4b` const + entry in `Dispatchable` list; (h) `HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs` gains keyed factory forwarder; (i) `.Worker\Program.cs` gains concrete DI registrations (Options bind, seam Singletons, handler Scoped); (j) `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests\Handlers\H4bBulkAppSettingsHandlerTests.cs` with hand-rolled fakes covering: full-manifest happy path, /healthz-never-green quarantine with parsed diagnostic, required-per-env-input-missing quarantine, PS-script-non-zero-exit quarantine, idempotency, cleartext leak scan; (k) `HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests` still passes; (l) `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` + `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/` + `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` all exit 0.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
Per lessons-learned-model1-prod-standup-2026-08-22.md finding F20/F20a + Automation Gaps roadmap item 13 in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md`: BFF container exits with code 134 (SIGABRT) at startup with `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException: SpeAdmin:KeyVaultUri (or KeyVaultUri) configuration is required for SpeAdminModule.` This is one of ~40 `.ValidateOnStart()` chains — each missing config surfaces as fail-fast in sequence. SESSION 2 observed the pattern after fixing F20 (added `SpeAdmin__KeyVaultUri`), next fail-fast was `CosmosPersistence:Endpoint` (F20a), and chose NOT to serially chase 40-module chain.

**The right fix**: set ALL required app settings in ONE batch call. **SESSION 4 recon revealed**: `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` (task 084 shipped output) ALREADY does this — batched `az webapp config appsettings set --settings @settings` per slot, driven from manifest. So task 201's original SESSION 3 design (author brand-new handler + new manifest + new generator) was 70% redundant. **What's actually missing**: per-env LITERAL App Service settings that DON'T come from KV — e.g., `SpeAdmin__KeyVaultUri` = `https://sprk-{env}-kv.vault.azure.net/` (a URI; storing in KV creates circular boot); `AzureAd__TenantId` = `<guid>` (public info, not a secret); `SharePointEmbedded__ContainerTypeId` = `<guid>` (public ID). Existing generator emits ONLY KV-ref-shaped values.

**Option A design (SESSION 4)**: Extend the SAME manifest with `per_env_settings:` top-level list; generator learns to emit these into the SAME `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` output alongside KV refs. H4b becomes thin: resolve per-env values from run state, shell to generated script, poll /healthz. Advantages: (1) preserves task 084's single source of truth, (2) reuses existing batched-write mechanism, (3) new BFF setting tomorrow = 1 manifest entry + 0 handler changes.

**Per-env inputs enumerated (initial set, extensible)** — resolved from HandlerEnvelope.Parameters.NonSecret populated by prior handlers:
| Manifest key | Per-env source | Comes from |
|---|---|---|
| `SpeAdmin__KeyVaultUri` | `from-h2a-output:kv_vault_uri` | H2a Bicep output |
| `AzureAd__TenantId` | `from-h0-parameter:tenant_id` | H0 preflight |
| `AzureAd__ClientId` | `from-h3-output:bff_app_client_id` | H3 Entra app-reg |
| `SharePointEmbedded__ContainerTypeId` | `from-h8-output:container_type_id` | H8 SPE creation |
| `SharePointEmbedded__WebhookSigningKey` | `from-h8-output:webhook_signing_key` | H8 SPE creation |
| `SharePointEmbedded__WebhookClientState` | `from-h8-output:webhook_client_state` | H8 SPE creation |
| `EmailProcessing__WebhookSigningKey` | `from-h14-output:email_webhook_signing_key` | H14 Exchange sidecar |
| `CosmosPersistence__Endpoint` | `from-h2a-output:cosmos_endpoint` | H2a Bicep output |
| ... (extended per BFF IOptions inventory) | | |

**BFF IOptions inventory** (~40 modules × ~2-4 settings each ≈ 80-160 total app settings). Enumeration during Step 2 of this task: `grep -r "ValidateOnStart" src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/` yields the full list. Each module's `.Bind(Configuration.GetSection("X"))` + validator field list defines what's required. Manifest source-of-truth for the full inventory: `docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md` § App Service settings (add-to during Step 2).

**L2 project layout confirmed via recon 2026-08-24**: handlers live in `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core\Handlers\<Family>\`. H4b will be in new folder `BulkAppSettings\`. Seams + impls co-located. Tests in `.Tests\Handlers\` (flat folder) using xunit + FluentAssertions + hand-rolled fakes.

**CLUSTER FINDING (from SESSION 2)**: F17 + F19 + F20 share ONE root cause — Bicep provisions Model 1 Prod infra but does NOT seed BFF runtime state. H4-shared (task 200) + H4b (this task) + H9 (task 052) together close this gap. Sequencing: H4-shared || H4-per-tenant → H4b → H9 → BFF starts configured (kills F20 progressive fail-fast permanently).
    </background>
