  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Single `IProvisioningHandler` implementation returning `Task&lt;HandlerResult&gt;`. Domain failures are `HandlerResult.Failure(FailureClass, RejectionCode, Diagnostic)` — do NOT throw exceptions for expected failure modes (PS non-zero exit, /healthz never green, required per-env input missing).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register in L2 control-plane, NOT BFF. Handler in `.Core`; concrete DI in `.Worker\Program.cs`; keyed forwarder in `.Core\Handlers\HandlerDispatchRegistrationModule.cs`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth ceremony 21 MUSTs. App Service `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` MUST already be set to UAMI resource ID BEFORE H4b writes KV-ref-shaped settings (F16 remediation gate). H4b's post-condition `/healthz` probe implicitly verifies — if KV refs can't resolve, /healthz stays red and H4b quarantines.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Reuse background-job infrastructure; return `HandlerResult`; fire-and-forget from L2 dispatcher.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key: `appsettings-{env}-{manifestVer}` — manifestVer is manifest hash from canonical secret-catalog (includes per_env_settings list).</constraint>
    <constraint source="Option-A-design-2026-08-24">Manifest extension is a NEW top-level list `per_env_settings:` (sibling to existing `secrets:`), NOT a modification of existing secret entries. Schema per entry: `key` (App Service app-setting name with `__` for nested config, e.g. `SpeAdmin__KeyVaultUri`), `per_env_source` (string in format `from-{handler}-output:{key}` or `from-{handler}-parameter:{key}` or `literal`), `literal_value?` (string; required only when `per_env_source == literal`), `iOptionsModule` (string documentation: which BFF module consumes this — for the IOptions audit report), `required` (bool, default true — required-and-missing = QuarantineRequired), `notes?` (string documentation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="Option-A-design-2026-08-24">Generator extension: `Test-ManifestShape` validates `per_env_settings:` top-level list (`ContainsKey` inclusive check per existing pattern); for each entry, validates required fields; conditionally validates `literal_value` present when `per_env_source == literal`. Generator emits per-env lines into the SAME `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` alphabetically-sorted, appended AFTER the KV-ref lines (still in the single `$settings = @( ... )` array so batched call is unaffected). New generator params on Configure script signature: one parameter per unique `from-{handler}-{key}` source (script becomes `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1 -VaultName X -AppServiceName Y -TenantId Z -KeyVaultUri A -ContainerTypeId B ...`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="Option-A-design-2026-08-24">Determinism preserved: `-Verify` MUST exit 0 after task lands. Two runs of generator against unchanged manifest MUST produce byte-identical outputs. Sort order: existing alphabetical by canonical name for `secrets:`; NEW alphabetical by `key` for `per_env_settings:`; both merged alphabetically in the single Configure script.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Option-A-design-2026-08-24">H4b handler is a thin wrapper — MUST NOT reimplement the batched-write logic. Handler: (1) resolves per-env values from HandlerEnvelope.Parameters.NonSecret; (2) shells to `pwsh` invoking generated Configure script with resolved args; (3) polls /healthz via IHealthzProbe (backoff 30s/60s/90s/120s/180s = 8 min); (4) on failure fetches container docker logs via KuduContainerLogFetcher + parses for fail-fast module name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Option-A-design-2026-08-24">Diff-first idempotency is preserved by the generator+script pattern: the shipped Configure script already batches ALL setting writes (KV-refs + new per-env), and Azure App Service natively de-dups (setting a value that already matches is a no-op that DOES trigger restart trigger — mitigate by pre-comparing via `az webapp config appsettings list` inside the script OR accepting the restart-once cost). Recommendation for this task: accept the restart-once cost (the whole POINT is applying all settings at once = ONE restart cycle); optimization for pure NO-OP scenario is future work.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Per-env-input resolution: H4b reads `per_env_source` field from manifest, then looks up the referenced key in `envelope.Parameters.NonSecret[key]`. If a required per-env-input is MISSING (prior handler didn't emit it), fail with `HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "PerEnvInputMissing", diagnostic naming source-handler + missing key)` BEFORE any script invocation. Surfaces upstream handler gaps early.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Post-condition `/healthz` probe: HttpHealthzProbe polls `https://{appServiceName}.azurewebsites.net/healthz` with backoff schedule 30s/60s/90s/120s/180s (5 probes; 8-min budget). Success = HTTP 200. Failure = fetch container docker logs via KuduContainerLogFetcher (Kudu API `/api/logs/docker`); parse for `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException:` line → extract IOptions module name → `HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "HealthzTimeout", "BFF fail-fast on {moduleName}: {message}")`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BINDING guard: manifest MUST NOT list Dataverse-ClientSecret or BFF-API-ClientSecret as `per_env_settings` entries — those secrets are KV-only (per `secrets:` list, `never_delete: true`). Generator `Test-ManifestShape` enforces at validation-time. Prevents an operator from accidentally writing a cleartext BFF client secret as an app-setting literal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md NFR-05">BFF /health must fail fast at boot on any Tier-1 IOptions misconfig — H4b's `/healthz` post-condition IS this check applied at H4b's timeframe. If /healthz fails, manifest is incomplete + must be extended (subsequent PR).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§10">L2 handlers register in L2 DI, NOT in BFF (§10 BFF Hygiene).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§11">NEW-surface justification field completed per §11 three-question gate (see &lt;justification&gt; below). H4b is a NEW handler primitive; per_env_settings is a NEW top-level manifest list; both justified per SESSION 4 recon (existing Configure script only handles KV refs; per-env-literal gap is real).</constraint>
  </constraints>

