  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a full manifest (secrets + per_env_settings) + all per-env-inputs present in envelope.Parameters.NonSecret, when HandleAsync runs, then IProcessRunner is invoked ONCE with generated Configure script + all resolved args; IHealthzProbe returns Success within backoff budget; result is HandlerResult.Success.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Required-per-env-input-missing Quarantine: given manifest requires `TenantId` per-env-input but envelope.Parameters.NonSecret doesn't have it, HandleAsync returns HandlerResult.Failure(Resumable, "PerEnvInputMissing", "TenantId (upstream handler H0 did not emit)") BEFORE any process invocation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PS non-zero exit: given IProcessRunner returns exit 1 with stderr, HandleAsync returns HandlerResult.Failure(Resumable, "AppSettingsWriteFailed", diagnostic containing exit code + stderr).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/healthz-never-green Quarantine with parsed diagnostic: given IHealthzProbe returns Timeout AND IContainerLogFetcher returns log containing `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException: SpeAdmin:KeyVaultUri`, HandleAsync returns HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "HealthzTimeout", "BFF fail-fast on SpeAdmin: ...").</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/healthz-never-green Quarantine with unparseable log: given Timeout + docker log with no fail-fast line, HandleAsync returns HandlerResult.Failure(QuarantineRequired, "HealthzTimeout", generic diagnostic including "check container docker logs").</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BINDING guard: given tampered manifest with `Dataverse-ClientSecret` in `per_env_settings` list, generator `Test-ManifestShape` fails with "BindingViolation: Dataverse-ClientSecret MUST be secrets: entry with never_delete:true, NOT per_env_settings" BEFORE any output is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-key match: two invocations for the same (env, manifestVer) — second call short-circuits before manifest read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Generator determinism: `-Verify` exits 0 after manifest + generator + Configure script regen.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Generator emits ONE batched call: inspect regenerated Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1 — verify all settings (KV refs + per_env literals) accumulate into single `$settings` array; single `az webapp config appsettings set --settings @settings` call per slot.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI via 3-file dance; HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` + `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/` + `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` all exit 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler catalog in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md` Step 3 enumeration lists H4b row accurately.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sequencing: H4b runs AFTER H4-shared (task 200) + AFTER H4 (task 047) AND BEFORE H9 (task 052) in L2 state machine DAG.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: lessons-learned-model1-prod-standup-2026-08-22.md finding F20/F20a + Automation Gaps roadmap item 13 + spec.md FR-36 canonical-manifest + NFR-05 fail-fast + design.md §4.1 H4 (sibling handler shape). Companion task: 200 (H4-shared).

## POML v2 rewrite (2026-08-24 SESSION 4) — Option A design lock-in

**Original SESSION 3 POML (commit 1b54beaa9) was 70% redundant** — corrected in this rewrite per SESSION 4 recon + discussion:

1. **Recon revealed**: task 084's shipped `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` ALREADY does batched `az webapp config appsettings set --settings @settings` per slot. My original design (author brand-new handler + new manifest + new generator + new writer) was 70% redundant.

2. **The real gap**: per-env LITERAL App Service settings (URIs, TenantId, ContainerTypeId, WebhookSigningKey — things not appropriate as KV secrets OR needed to bootstrap KV access). Existing generator emits KV refs ONLY.

3. **Option A design chosen** (user confirmed 2026-08-24): extend task 084's manifest with NEW top-level list `per_env_settings:`. Generator emits per-env lines into SAME `Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1`. H4b becomes THIN wrapper (~100 lines): resolve per-env values, shell to pwsh, poll /healthz, parse docker logs on failure.

4. **Handler file paths** — corrected `.Core\Handlers\BulkAppSettings\` (was imagined single-project path).

5. **HandlerResult contract** — corrected `Task&lt;HandlerResult&gt;` return type (was assumed exception-based).

6. **Sibling manifest option REJECTED**: I originally proposed `scripts/canonical-app-settings/` sibling manifest; user + I agreed this re-creates the drift task 084 was created to eliminate.

**Design decisions locked in via SESSION 4 discussion + user AskUserQuestion**:
- Extension is ADDITIVE new top-level list (safe per recon confirming 085/086 only read `canonical_name` + `aliases`)
- Handler is THIN (shells to generated PS) — pattern break from H4 SDK-based writer, but well-defined + testable
- Preserves task 084's single source of truth
- New BFF settings tomorrow = 1 manifest entry + 0 handler changes

**Follow-on task (NOT in scope)**: If pattern break of shelling to pwsh is judged too much of a smell later, follow-on task could extend generator to ALSO emit `.cs` codegen (`AppSettingsWiring.generated.cs`) alongside `.ps1`, and H4b links against it (SDK-native pattern). Deferred; document as design consideration.

**Coordination with task 200**: Both tasks modify `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` + `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1`. Land task 200 FIRST (smaller extension: enum value + optional field). Then task 201 extends with new top-level list. Avoids merge conflict.
  </notes>

